    "notes": "Detailed 425 m completed architectural exterior accepted for world-viewer use: two-tone aluminum piers and recessed double glazing, three flared light-dish bands, external paired panoramic lifts, pale upper wings, 45 m four-point folded aluminum crown with panel seams and internal braces, granite base and glazed entry. Intermediate facade datums, crown shoulder slopes, fine ACP module, bracing and street vestibule are reconstructed from NEB, Sheffield developer plans, Skyart fabrication evidence and the credited completed exterior photograph. Hotel occupancy, interiors, basements and neighboring structures are excluded."
